    "en":  {
               "headline":  "Strong Q3 overshadowed as AI sell-off drags ANET below its 200-day EMA",
               "technical":  "On 20 Nov 2026 ANET opened near $185.09 and closed at $167.62 (−11.59%) on 13.83M shares, about 1.5× its 20-day average of 9.12M. That much volume means the selling was real. Trend: price is now below all three EMAs (exponential moving averages, which are smoothed trend lines): EMA50 $187.49, EMA100 $184.06 and EMA200 $171.67. The EMAs are still in bullish order (50 \u003e 100 \u003e 200), so the longer uptrend is bent but not broken. Still, closing below the EMA200 is a clear warning. Momentum: MACD (a trend-momentum gauge) is −0.92, slightly above its signal line at −1.19, with a small positive histogram of +0.26. Momentum was flat before the drop and has not yet turned clearly negative. RSI 14 (a 0–100 momentum gauge; under 30 is oversold) is 41.47: weak but not oversold. Price sits in the bottom fifth of the Bollinger Bands (a 20-day volatility band: lower $158.04, middle $182.15, upper $206.25). It is 22.9% below the 52-week high of $217.41 and about halfway between that high and the $114.52 low. Nearby support is around $158. Resistance is first at $171.67, then the $182–187 zone.",
               "fundamental":  "Arista sells high-speed switches, but its real edge is EOS, the software that runs AI and cloud data-center networks. Q3 2026, reported on 3 Nov, was its fastest growth since its IPO. Revenue was $3.66B, up 58.5% year on year and about 10% above its own $3.3B guidance. Non-GAAP gross margin was 64.0% and operating margin 49.1%. Q4 guidance is $3.9–4.0B, with non-GAAP EPS of $1.26–1.30. Management raised its 2026 revenue forecast to about $13.3B (+48%). It also gave a first 2027 view of about $18.5B (+38–40%), with AI-fabric revenue roughly doubling to about $7B, and said it has more than 100 Etherlink customers. Gross margin is guided at 62–64% while revenue scales, which suggests EOS still commands software-like pricing. That pricing power is the core of the moat. Watch points: inventory rose to $3.2B and purchase commitments to $11.4B as Arista locks in memory and optics supply.",
               "news":  [
                            "3 Nov 2026: Q3 revenue was $3.66B (+58.5% YoY), with non-GAAP EPS of $1.20, gross margin of 64.0% and operating margin of 49.1%. Q4 guidance is $3.9–4.0B revenue and EPS of $1.26–1.30.",
                            "On the Q3 call, management raised its 2026 revenue forecast to about $13.3B (+48%) and gave an initial 2027 outlook of about $18.5B (+38–40%), with AI fabrics expected to reach about $7B. It also flagged supply constraints and rising memory costs, and purchase commitments grew to $11.4B.",
                            "Also in the Q3 release, Arista announced open, standards-based rack-scale AI networking designs with AMD, Arm, Broadcom, Meta, Microsoft and Qualcomm. Its Etherlink SU-144 design connects up to 144 accelerators per rack in a single hop.",
                            "Analysts stayed positive after the results. JPMorgan raised its target to $270 from $250 on 4 Nov, and Evercore ISI kept an Outperform rating with a $250 target on 19 Nov. MarketBeat\u0027s consensus target across 25 firms was about $240 as of 19 Nov.",
                            "20 Nov 2026: ANET fell 11.59% in a broad AI sell-off. The Nasdaq dropped 5.28%, Nvidia fell 14.01%, and the S\u0026P 500 entered correction territory. The sources reviewed named no Arista-specific news; the backdrop included Nvidia\u0027s CEO change (reported by AP on 17 Nov) and Anthropic\u0027s weak second trading day."
                        ],
               "caution":  "The 20 Nov drop was a market-wide event, but it exposes real risks. ANET trades at a premium, around 50× earnings according to TradingKey, so any sign of cloud companies cutting spending can shrink that multiple quickly. Microsoft and Meta reportedly make up about 42% of revenue. The $11.4B in purchase commitments, plus rising memory costs, could squeeze margins if demand cools. Nvidia\u0027s Spectrum-X Ethernet competes directly with Arista. On the chart, a close below the $158 lower Bollinger Band would point to further weakness, and the wider market correction may not be over.",
               "opportunity":  "Nothing in the business broke on 20 Nov. There was no guidance cut and no customer loss, and analysts still held positive views as late as 19 Nov (Evercore, Outperform). Management has already guided 2027 to about $18.5B, with AI-fabric revenue roughly doubling. Arista also has growing open-Ethernet partnerships with AMD, Broadcom, Meta and Microsoft. For long-term holders, a market-driven drop in a company with 49% operating margins can be a time to review the position against the thesis. Watch whether price can climb back above $171.67 (EMA200).",
               "risks":  [
